      SELECT vfs_entries.entry_id, vfs_entries.content_hash, vfs_entries.created_at, vfs_entries.deleted_at, vfs_entries.kind, vfs_entries.mime_type, vfs_en
      SELECT vfs_entries.parent_id, vfs_entries.content_hash, vfs_entries.created_at, vfs_entries.deleted_at, vfs_entries.kind, vfs_entries.mime_type, vfs_e

== 3. the plan SQLite picks for a children listing with the liveness term
  children of one parent, live only, by name: ['SEARCH vfs_entries USING INDEX sqlite_autoindex_vfs_entries_1 (parent_id=?)']
  children of one parent, tombstoned only: ['SEARCH vfs_entries USING INDEX sqlite_autoindex_vfs_entries_1 (parent_id=?)']
  every tombstoned root: ['SCAN vfs_entries USING INDEX ix_vfs_entries_path']
  every tombstoned root, as the retention sweep asks: ['SCAN vfs_entries USING INDEX ix_vfs_entries_path']

== 4. the trash view over 7,000 tombstoned roots
  ls /.vfs/trash as system: rows returned=7000 statements=3 vm_steps=168547
